      {
        "section_number": "5.1",
        "title": "Definition of OSI based services",
        "content_preview": "\nISO 15118-2 is based on the conventions discussed in the OSI Service Conventions (refer to ISO 10731) as they apply for the individual layers specified in this document. \n\nThis part of ISO 15118-2 describes requirements applicable to layer 3-7 according to the OSI layered architecture. \n",
        "content_length": 289,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "functional",
        "test_importance": "medium",
        "requirements": [],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "5.2",
        "title": "Requirement structure",
        "content_preview": "\nThis document uses a requirement structure i.e. a unique number identifies each individual requirement included in this document. This requirement structure allows for easier requirement tracking and test case specification. The following format is used: \n\n\"[V2G\"Y\"-\"XXX\"]\" requirement text Where: \n\n \"V2G\" represents the ISO 15118 set of standards, \n\n Y represents the document part of the ISO 15118 document set \n\n XXX represents the individual requirement number and \n\n\"requirement text\" inclu...",
        "content_length": 600,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "normative",
        "test_importance": "medium",
        "requirements": [
          "V2G2-000"
        ],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
