      {
        "section_number": "7.2.1",
        "title": "Overview",
        "content_preview": "\nThis subclause explains how the OSI layered architecture is applied for the purpose of this document. It is intended to provide simple means for describing the interfaces between the individual communication protocol layers required by this document and furthermore allows for defining timing requirements more precisely. \n\nServices are specified by describing the service primitives and parameters that characterize a service. This is an abstract definition of services and does not force a particu...",
