      {
        "section_number": "7.3.3",
        "title": "Number of root certificates and root validity, certificate depth and size",
        "content_preview": "\n[V2G2-008] Each EVCC shall support at least one V2G Root Certificate. \n\n[V2G2-877] Each SECC shall support the storage of at least 10 V2G Root Certificates. \n\nNOTE 1 Due to overlapping validity periods, up to 10 concurrently valid certificates may exist. See V2G2-012 \n\nNOTE 2 A number of five (5) V2G Root Certificates is strongly recommended. However, just one is mandatory. Having less than 5 or just 1 certificate brings a risk to the OEM. Having just 1 V2G Root Certificate allows the car to ch...",
