        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "7.6.2.2",
        "title": "Dynamic Host Control Protocol (DHCPV6)",
        "content_preview": "\nData-link requirements are described in Part 3 of this standard. The EVCC starts the address assignment triggered by the data-link when a data-link connection is established. This is done according to subclause 7.6.3.2 using SLAAC, which is mandatory according to this standard. DHCPv6 might be implemented as an optional IP configuration method. \n\n[V2G2-043] If an EVCC chooses to implement a DHCPv6 client it shall implement it according to IETF RFC 3315. \n\n[V2G2-044] If the infrastructure the EV...",
        "content_length": 613,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "functional",
        "test_importance": "high",
        "requirements": [
          "V2G2-044",
          "V2G2-043"
        ],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "7.6.2.3",
        "title": "Neighbor Discovery (ND)",
        "content_preview": "\nThe EVCC uses IPv6 stateless address auto configuration for generating addresses for its interface. All interfaces have a link-local address. To ensure unique addresses and to support global addresses the neighbour discovery protocol is used. \n\n[V2G2-045] The EVCC shall implement neigborhood discovery as defined in IETF RFC 4861. \n\n[V2G2-046] The EVCC shall comply with IETF RFC 4429 allowing assignment of IP addresses before Duplicate Address Detection is finished. \n",
        "content_length": 472,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "general",
        "test_importance": "high",
        "requirements": [
          "V2G2-046",
          "V2G2-045"
        ],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "7.6.2.4",
        "title": "Internet Control Message Protocol (ICMP)",
        "content_preview": "\nThe Internet Control Message Protocol (ICMP) is used to send error messages (e.g. a requested service is not available, a host could not be reached etc.). \n\n[V2G2-047] Each V2G Entity shall implement ICMPv6 as specified in IETF RFC 4443. \n\n[V2G2-049] Each V2G Entity shall implement the RFCs referred to in column 'Reference' of Table 5 describing the implementation details for the respective ICMP message type. \n\n\nTable 5 — Mandatory ICMP Message Set\n\n\n<table><tr><td>ICMP message type</td><td>ICM...",
        "content_length": 1501,
        "level": 1,
