      {
        "section_number": "7.7.3.1",
        "title": "Overview",
        "content_preview": "\nSecurity on Transport Layer is being provided by using TLS. This allows to establish an authenticated and encrypted (ensures integrity protection and confidentiality protection) channel between the EVCC and the SECC. TLS allows for unilateral or mutual authentication. For ISO 15118 security it was agreed to use unilateral authentication (the EVCC authenticates the SECC). \n",
        "content_length": 376,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "general",
        "test_importance": "high",
        "requirements": [],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "7.7.3.2",
        "title": "Applicable RFCs",
        "content_preview": "\n[V2G2-067] For the considered use cases unilateral authentication with TLS version 1.2 according to IETF RFC 5246 with extensions according to IETF RFC 6066 shall be supported by each V2G Entity. The EVCC authenticates the SECC by verifying the SECC Certificate (chain) provided from the SECC to the EVCC. \n\nWith unilateral authentication the EVCC authenticates the SECC according to [V2G2-067] , which can also be used to protect the cyclic meter reading between the SECC and the EVCC. Application ...",
        "content_length": 1391,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "general",
        "test_importance": "high",
        "requirements": [
          "V2G2-067"
        ],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "7.7.3.3",
        "title": "Transport Layer Security Usage",
        "content_preview": "\n[V2G2-068] The SECC shall always act as the TLS server component. \n\n[V2G2-070] Each EVCC shall check the validity of the Sub-CA Certificates (in the SECCs certificate chain) via an OCSP response according to IETF RFC 6960, when TLS is used. The OCSP Requests \n\nshall be transported as part of the TLS handshake using the extension defined in IETF RFC 6961. \n\nNOTE 1 It is not intended, that the EVCC requests an OCSP response for an SECC leaf certificate during TLS handshake. \n\nA \"pairing mode\" sup...",
        "content_length": 5324,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "functional",
        "test_importance": "high",
        "requirements": [
          "V2G2-649",
          "V2G2-651",
