      {
        "section_number": "7.8.1",
        "title": "General Information",
        "content_preview": "\nThe V2G Transfer Protocol (V2GTP) is a compact communication protocol to transfer V2G messages between two V2GTP entities. It mainly consist of a header and payload definition that allows to separate and process V2G messages efficiently. V2GTP is the standard transfer protocol between the EVCC and SECC but may also be used for communication with other V2G Entities that support the V2GTP protocol. \n",
        "content_length": 402,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "general",
        "test_importance": "high",
        "requirements": [],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "7.8.2",
        "title": "Supported ports",
        "content_preview": "\nV2GTP is based on TLS+TCP. TLS+TCP uses a pair of IP addresses (source address and destination address) and a pair of port numbers (source port and destination port) to establish and identify a connection for bidirectional exchange of byte streams. The connection is established from the source address and source port to the destination address and destination port. The ports listed in Table 8 are used by V2GTP entities. \n\n\nTable 8 — Supported TCP ports for V2GTP\n\n\n<table><tr><td>Name</td><td>Pr...",
        "content_length": 2477,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "general",
        "test_importance": "high",
        "requirements": [
          "V2G2-081",
          "V2G2-076",
