      {
        "section_number": "7.10.1.1",
        "title": "General Information",
        "content_preview": "\nAn EVCC uses the SECC Discover Protocol (SDP) to get the IP address and port number of the SECC. The SDP client sends out SECC Discovery Request messages to the local link (multicast) expecting any SDP server to answer its request with a SECC Discovery Response message containing this information. \n\nAfter the EVCC received the IP address and the port number of the SECC, it can establish a transport layer connection to the SECC (refer to subclause 7.3.4). \n\n[V2G2-123] An SDP server shall be acce...",
        "content_length": 778,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "general",
        "test_importance": "high",
        "requirements": [
          "V2G2-123"
        ],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "7.10.1.2",
        "title": "Supported ports",
        "content_preview": "\nSDP is a UDP based protocol. The ports listed in Table 15 are used by SDP. \n\n\nTable 15 — Supported UDP ports for SDP\n\n\n<table><tr><td>Name</td><td>Protocol</td><td>Port number</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td>V2G_UTP_UTPCLIENT</td><td>UDP (unicast)</td><td>Port number in the range of Dynamic Ports (49152-65535) as defined in IETF RFC 6335.</td><td>SDP client source port at the EVCC</td></tr><tr><td>V2G_UTP_UTPSERVER</td><td>UDP (multicast)</td><td>15118</td><td>SDP server port which accepts...",
        "content_length": 1411,
