      {
        "section_number": "8.1",
        "title": "General information and definitions",
        "content_preview": "\nA V2G message uses the EXI-based Presentation Layer as described in 7.9.1. The communication between EVCC and SECC at application layer level is based on a client/server architecture. The EVCC always acts as a client (service requester) during the entire charging process, whereas the SECC always acts as a server (service responder). Hence the EVCC always initiates communication by sending a request message to the SECC which then returns the corresponding response message. All messages exchanged...",
        "content_length": 1414,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "general",
        "test_importance": "high",
        "requirements": [
          "V2G2-809"
        ],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
