        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "8.4.5.3.2",
        "title": "PreChargeReq",
        "content_preview": "\nThe PreChargeReq is used to start the Pre Charge process from EV side. \n\n[V2G2-253] Depending on the selected Message Set(s) as defined in subclause 8.6.2, the EVCC and the SECC shall implement the mandatory messages and message elements as in Table 104 and according to Figure 51. \n\n![image](https://cdn-mineru.openxlab.org.cn/result/2026-03-18/ef87c0e3-acd6-46d4-bc33-443a4314ecab/14d4b2e57d0332d5d7cebba866ac0fb9c209ed4467e6336ec3f67269fbd9f3f4.jpg)\n\n\n\nFigure 51 — Schema Diagram – PreChargeReq\n\n...",
        "content_length": 1121,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "functional",
        "test_importance": "high",
        "requirements": [
          "V2G2-254",
          "V2G2-253"
        ],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "8.4.5.3.3",
        "title": "PreChargeRes",
        "content_preview": "\nAfter receiving the PreChargeReq from the EVCC the SECC sends the PreChargeRes informing the EV about the EVSE status and the present EVSE output voltage. \n\n[V2G2-255] Depending on the selected Message Set(s) as defined in subclause 8.6.2, the EVCC and the SECC shall implement the mandatory messages and message elements as defined in Table 104 and according to Figure 52. \n\n![image](https://cdn-mineru.openxlab.org.cn/result/2026-03-18/ef87c0e3-acd6-46d4-bc33-443a4314ecab/49f4d2e991b5faef4985fc60...",
        "content_length": 1346,
        "level": 1,
