      {
        "section_number": "8.4.5.4.1",
        "title": "CurrentDemandReq/Res Handling",
        "content_preview": "\nFor DC charging control cyclic exchange of the requested current from EV side is necessary. Also the target voltage and the difference in current and voltages is transferred. \n",
        "content_length": 177,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "functional",
        "test_importance": "high",
        "requirements": [],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "8.4.5.4.2",
        "title": "CurrentDemandReq",
        "content_preview": "\nBy sending the CurrentDemandReq the EV requests a certain current from the EVSE. Also the target voltage, current and voltage difference are transferred. \n\n[V2G2-257] Depending on the selected Message Set(s) as defined in subclause 8.6.2, the EVCC and the SECC shall implement the mandatory messages and message elements as defined in Table 104 and according to Figure 53. \n\n![image](https://cdn-mineru.openxlab.org.cn/result/2026-03-18/ef87c0e3-acd6-46d4-bc33-443a4314ecab/9057afa451ac0c79f3f118ceb...",
        "content_length": 2466,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "functional",
        "test_importance": "high",
        "requirements": [
          "V2G2-258",
          "V2G2-257"
        ],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "8.4.5.4.3",
        "title": "CurrentDemandRes",
        "content_preview": "\nAfter receiving the CurrentDemandReq from the EVCC the SECC sends the CurrentDemandRes informing the EV about the EVSE status and the present EVSE output voltage and current. \n\n[V2G2-259] Depending on the selected Message Set(s) as defined in subclause 8.6.2, the EVCC and the SECC shall implement the mandatory messages and message elements as defined in Table 104 and according to Figure 54. \n\n![image](https://cdn-mineru.openxlab.org.cn/result/2026-03-18/ef87c0e3-acd6-46d4-bc33-443a4314ecab/04e4...",
        "content_length": 4019,
