      {
        "section_number": "8.7.1",
        "title": "Overview",
        "content_preview": "\nThis subclause describes the timing and error handling for the V2G Communication Session. The error handling is based on timers enabling the EVCC and the SECC to monitor the V2G message exchange. For the detection of missing or delayed messages the EVCC and the SECC use predefined timeout values as error criteria. Whenever a timer is equal of larger than the related timeout the related error handling is processed. \n\nA timer counts the duration from the last time it was reset and then started. T...",
