      {
        "section_number": "8.7.4.1",
        "title": "Overview",
        "content_preview": "\nISO 15118 based charging control extends the IEC 61861-1 signaled charging. For this, the messaging on application layer is synchronised with the CP States defined in IEC 61851-1. \n\nISO 15118 based messaging is able to manage the AC and DC charging process for a complete charging - session from the beginning to the end in $5 \\%$ duty cycle case. \n\nFor AC, ISO 15118 also allows to start charging based on IEC 61851-1 (Basic Charging, BC) and switch to ``-`-` ISO 15118 based charging control (High...",
        "content_length": 2155,
