      {
        "section_number": "8.8.1",
        "title": "Overview",
        "content_preview": "\nIn a V2G Communication Session the EVCC and the SECC exchange Request-Response Message Pairs based on a predefined sequence. In this document this is referenced as Request-Response Message Sequence. These Request-Response Message Sequences allow both sides to synchronize the process in any situation and to control the communication between two V2G Entities. \n\nThe basic error handling concept in ISO 15118 is based on application level timers for Request-Response Message Sequences. This enables a...",
