      {
        "section_number": "",
        "title": "I.1 Overview",
        "content_preview": "\nThis chapter gives message sequence examples to make the comprehension of the renegotiation mechanism easier. \n\nIn ISO 15118-2, the renegotiation mechanism is used to change charge target settings and scheduling during a charging loop. Renegotiation can be initiated either by the EVCC or SECC. \n\nTo initiate a renegotiation by the SECC, the SECC has to set EVSENotification in EVSEStatus to 'ReNegotiation'. If so, the EVCC shall initiate a renegotiation in a limited time (see also [V2G2-680]). \n\n...",
        "content_length": 1248,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "general",
        "test_importance": "",
        "requirements": [
          "V2G2-522",
          "V2G2-683",
          "V2G2-686",
          "V2G2-680"
        ],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "section_number": "",
        "title": "I.2 Renegotiation after resuming a V2G Communication Session",
        "content_preview": "\nThe renegotiation process is only allowed after a first successful negotiation. \n\nIf one of EVCC or SECC wants to perform a renegotiation after resuming a V2G Communication Session, they first have to go through the V2G messaging until PowerDeliveryReq/Res message pair and apply the corresponding renegotiation mechanism as described in this standard and in the two examples provided above. \n",
        "content_length": 394,
        "level": 1,
        "classification": "functional",
        "test_importance": "",
        "requirements": [],
        "is_message_def": false,
        "message_type": null,
        "fields": [],
        "timing_params": [],
        "children": []
      },
